From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:21:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: build the incremental-rendering FBD sets only when
 needed, share their frame shaders

get_fb_descs() builds, next to the pass's FBDs, three spare FBD sets for
incremental rendering (IR_FIRST/MIDDLE/LAST), which only the tiler OOM
handler reads. Each IR set ran cmd_get_frame_shaders() again, once per
layer, and each run re-emits the preload/resolve DCDs: a meta-cache shader
lookup, blend descriptors, a sampler, a resource table, a ZS descriptor,
FAUs and one texture descriptor per loaded target. A colour + D24S8 pass
that loads both built 4 frame-shader sets (8 preload DCDs) and 4 FBD sets;
a clear-only pass, which tiles nothing and so can't hit a tiler OOM, still
built all three IR sets.

- With no tiler context (render->tiler == 0, the clear-only path of
  CmdEndRendering, which ends the pass), the IR sets are skipped and their
  OOM-context pointers are 0. Every draw allocates the tiler context
  before the FBDs, so a pass that tiles anything still gets all three.
- The frame shaders depend only on (fb, load, resolve); the layer and the
  store don't enter cmd_get_frame_shaders(), and the DCDs are never
  patched. Without a resolve shader (modes[2] NEVER in the main set) the
  main set (fb.load, resolve) equals IR_FIRST's (fb.load, NULL), and
  IR_MIDDLE's (spill.load, NULL) equals IR_LAST's (spill.load, resolve):
  those reuse the same DCDs. With a resolve, each IR pass builds its own
  set as before. Either way once per IR pass, not once per layer.
- The IR FBD bodies (spill/final stores, CRC stripping on v10) are still
  emitted per IR pass and layer, unchanged.

Per pass, 1 layer, no resolve: load pass 8 -> 4 preload DCDs (4 -> 2
frame-shader sets), clear + draws 4 -> 2, clear-only 4 -> 0 DCDs and
4 -> 1 FBD sets. The FBD sets the OOM handler reads hold the same bytes
apart from DCD addresses whose contents are identical.

PANVK_NO_SPARE_FBD_REUSE=1 builds every IR set from scratch again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QAYrqSPd4TgpVaKLqz5cYR

Purpose: R4: CPU per render pass: the incremental-rendering (tiler-OOM) FBD sets are skipped for clear-only passes, IR_FIRST reuses the main set's frame shaders and IR_LAST IR_MIDDLE's when there is no resolve, and frame shaders are built once per IR pass instead of per layer. PANVK_NO_SPARE_FBD_REUSE=1 reverts
Upstream-commit: none
Tested GPU: Mali-G615 MC6 (Anbernic RG477M, Dimensity 8300, v11)
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21 / MediaTek
Dependencies: none; applies on the full g615-v11-csf series after rg477m/027 (same file as rg477m/024-027)
Validation test: drawcpu bench passes modes on the device: pass recording 4.99 -> 4.18 us/pass (LOAD/CLEAR mix, -16%) and 4.43 -> 3.89 (CLEAR, -12%); PanProbe 38/38 x2 on rpspare.so; ircheck colour and depth checksums identical across rpspare, drawcpu and base builds in all 4 variants, uncapped; the tiler-OOM path can't be exercised on this kernel (B15: the uAPI 1.21 group create has no csi_handlers, so a forced overflow terminates the group on every build); combined build next.so (15c3385bbe40, rg477m/023-037): PanProbe 38/38 x2 (unsafe profile 37/38, only the bc_decode raw readback, by design); 16-game boot sweep 2026-10-25 in quietd Stock mode: Hades 60, Jupiter Hell 59, Risk of Rain 2 38, Moonlighter 60, Megabonk 60, Portal 2 60, Gladius 60, Crysis 3 Remastered 60 fps; Arkham Asylum to the menu; Factorio and Ashes menus render as before; Descenders, Tomb Raider, Doom 3 BFG and Metro 2033 match their known states; 0 GPU faults; Serious Sam bot benchmark A-B-B-A compat 49.2/52.7 vs next 53.3/51.1 fps; Arkham Asylum 20-round interleaved A/B 2026-10-25 (quietd Stock), base rg477m vs next: launch failures 1/20 vs 0/20 (session total 1/33 vs 4/36, not significant; B5 signatures also seen on the stock driver), gameplay fps median 36.4 vs 36.5, speckcount on 3 gameplay frames per run 0-1 px in both arms (base 2 runs with 1 px, next 3 runs with 1 px; the old specks bug gave tens to hundreds): no specks
Channel: compatibility, unsafe
